NAME
    digest - calculate a normalized cryptographic or MD5 digest

SYNOPSIS
    digest -a <algorithm>
    digest -a <algorithm> -- <file>

DESCRIPTION
    digest calculates one digest from standard input or from one readable
    regular file and writes the lowercase hexadecimal digest followed by a
    newline.

    Supported algorithms are sha256, sha512 and md5.

    When no file operand is supplied, input is read from standard input.
    A file operand requires the -- delimiter.

    digest selects an available host backend for the requested algorithm and
    validates the returned digest before writing it.

OPTIONS
    -a <algorithm>
        Select sha256, sha512 or md5.

OPERANDS
    <file>
        Read digest input from this readable regular file.

ENVIRONMENT
    Requires a nonempty m_ROOT inherited from an initialized m environment.
    From an uninitialized host shell, invoke m digest [arguments].


EXIT STATUS
    0   Success.
    2   Invalid invocation or unsupported algorithm.
    Other non-zero status indicates input, backend or digest-validation failure.
